Link the -Wl,--version-script capability probe as a shared object.

On MidnightBSD (as on FreeBSD), crt1.o defines environ and __progname and
libc.so references them, so an executable linked with a version script that
localizes everything fails with both LLD and GNU ld:

  ld: error: non-exported symbol 'environ' in '/usr/lib/crt1.o' is referenced by DSO '/lib/libc.so.7'

The probe then reports "unsupported" and the project symbol-version maps are
never applied to the shared libraries. Mirrors the FreeBSD ports fix.

--- meson.build.orig	2026-06-03 14:42:00 UTC
+++ meson.build
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@ have_version_script = cc.links(
 meson_test_map = meson.current_source_dir() / 'test/meson_test.map'
 have_version_script = cc.links(
     'int main(void) { return 0; }',
-    args: f'-Wl,--version-script=@meson_test_map@',
+    args: ['-shared', f'-Wl,--version-script=@meson_test_map@'],
     name: '-Wl,--version-script',
 )
 
